@page "/components/slider"

<PageTitle>Slider — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Slider</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    <code>&lt;input type="range"&gt;</code>. Radix builds a slider from five divs, a pointer-event
    graph and a roving tab index, and spends most of that code reimplementing what the input
    already does — including the part that is never reimplemented correctly, announcing the value
    as it changes, in the user's own units.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="SliderExample.razor"><SliderExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Range</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    A lower and an upper bound is two inputs with two names, which is also what a server wants to
    read — so the honest shape and the useful one agree.
</p>
<Example Source="SliderRange.razor"><SliderRange /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Multiple Thumbs</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    There is no two-thumb control here, and the reason is that the input has one. Rebuilding it
    would mean rebuilding the drag, the arrow keys, the step grid and the announcement — which is
    exactly the code the platform is being used to avoid.
</p>
<Example Source="SliderMultipleThumbs.razor"><SliderMultipleThumbs /></Example>

